TITLE:: InsightPanel
summary:: the analyser's face: a header and a dashboard of titled panes
categories:: Libraries>Insight
related:: Classes/Insight, Classes/InsightGUI, Classes/InsightSpectrumView, Classes/InsightMeterView, Classes/InsightHistoryView, Classes/InsightImagerView, Classes/InsightReadingsView

DESCRIPTION::
What link::Classes/InsightGUI:: shows: the header every effect window has (FxHeader) and, below it, five panes - the spectrum, the levels and loudness, the loudness history, the stereo image and the readings since reset. No mix and no output: an analyser changes nothing, so there is nothing to mix.

table::
## strong::header:: || the power button runs the analysis; the presets are loudness targets (link::Classes/Insight#*presetNames::), each a target LUFS and a true peak ceiling; save keeps your own; code::...:: copies, pastes, goes back to the defaults; then freeze, reset and the bus (BusManager's names, a number, the channels)
## strong::spectrum:: || its source, tilt, speed, held trace and fft size along its top; drag up and down for the floor, a click clears the held trace
## strong::levels · loudness:: || a bar per channel (dBFS) and M and S (LUFS); drag the ceiling on the channels and the target on M and S; a click drops what is held
## strong::loudness · short term:: || one or five minutes; the target as an outlined band, the integrated loudness dotted; drag for the target
## strong::stereo:: || the goniometer, correlation, balance, width
## strong::since reset:: || the integrated loudness big, how far from the target, the rest of the numbers, the target and ceiling knobs
::

Signal blue for levels and spectra, the same blue paler for loudness (link::#*loud::), white for what is held, outlines for the targets (link::#*drawTarget::), red only for an over. Every pane says in the hint strip what is under the pointer.

code::
s.boot;
i = Insight(\main, 0, 2);
g = i.gui;
p = g.panel;
p.frozen = true;             // hold the picture, the analysis goes on
p.frozen = false;
p.sourceChoice.valueAction = 3;    // the spectrum of the mid
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: insight
The link::Classes/Insight:: to show.
ARGUMENT:: parent
A parent view, or nil.

METHOD:: loud
The colour of loudness (LUFS): the signal's blue, paler.

METHOD:: drawTarget
Draw a target the way every pane does: a faint band, its outline, a dashed line through its middle. Inside a drawFunc.
ARGUMENT:: rect
The band, as a Rect.

METHOD:: deltaText
How far a loudness is from a target, in words: code::"on the target"::, code::"6.5 LU under the target"::.
ARGUMENT:: lufs
The loudness.
ARGUMENT:: target
The target.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: view
The View, for a layout.

METHOD:: insight
The link::Classes/Insight:: shown.

METHOD:: header
The FxHeader.

METHOD:: frozen
Whether the picture is held. The analysis goes on underneath.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true holds it.

METHOD:: running
Whether the panes are being drawn (25 times a second). The window turns it on; it does not start or stop the analysis.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true draws.

METHOD:: refresh
Every control from the insight, and the panes drawn again.

METHOD:: widgets
The controls under the header, for dimming them while the analysis is off.

METHOD:: busText
What the bus button says: code::"bus 0 · 2 ch":: or the BusManager name followed.

METHOD:: hints
The hint strip the panel and its panes speak to.
ARGUMENT:: bar
An FxHintBar.

METHOD:: tickAction
A function called a couple of times a second while drawing: the window updates its footer from it.

METHOD:: remove
Stop drawing and listening. The window calls it when it closes.

METHOD:: isClosed
Whether the view is gone.

METHOD:: spectrumView
METHOD:: meterView
METHOD:: historyView
METHOD:: imagerView
METHOD:: readingsView
The panes.

